1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:01,569
Welcome to CutNest.

2
00:00:01,569 --> 00:00:02,848
In the next minute,

3
00:00:02,848 --> 00:00:08,098
I'll take a real sheet metal job from a
cut list to a finished customer quote.

4
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:10,490
First, pick the material.

5
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:15,126
Your library holds the sheet sizes
you buy and what you pay for them.

6
00:00:15,126 --> 00:00:18,687
This job is 2mm 316 brushed stainless.

7
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:23,692
Next, paste in the cut list, straight
from an email or a spreadsheet.

8
00:00:23,692 --> 00:00:27,137
CutNest reads most formats,
so there's no retyping.

9
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:29,394
Hit calculate.

10
00:00:29,394 --> 00:00:34,017
It's a brushed finish, so the grain
is locked and no part gets turned.

11
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:37,713
Here's exactly what to
order, and what it'll cost.

12
00:00:37,713 --> 00:00:42,327
2 sheets, and CutNest has proved
that no layout can do it in fewer.

13
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:44,600
Every sheet is drawn to scale,

14
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:49,720
with the parts labelled and any usable
offcuts marked, ready for the shop floor.

15
00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:51,761
Now turn it into a quote.

16
00:00:51,761 --> 00:00:55,549
With Pro, the cutting time
comes from the actual layout,

17
00:00:55,549 --> 00:00:57,511
at your own rates and markup.

18
00:00:57,511 --> 00:01:00,758
Add the customer, and any
extras, like delivery.

19
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:08,723
And there's your quote, on your own
letterhead, ready to print, or send as a PDF.

20
00:01:09,450 --> 00:01:13,714
CutNest is free to try in your
browser, with no account.

21
00:01:13,714 --> 00:01:15,999
Head to cutnest.co.uk.
